[236] indent=0 block=-
[237] indent=4 block=36bdbe27
      "▾ "
      "Good"
[238] indent=6 block=36bdbe27
      "Question:" {b}
      " "
[239] indent=0 block=-
[240] indent=6 block=36bdbe27
      "\"For ERCOT operating day 2026-05-15, why are LMPs forecast so low " {i}
[241] indent=6 block=36bdbe27
      "in DA at HB_WEST?\"" {i}
[242] indent=0 block=-
[243] indent=6 block=36bdbe27
      "Response: " {b}
[244] indent=0 block=-
[245] indent=6 block=36bdbe27
      "“The short answer: a classic West Texas renewable oversupply " {i}
[246] indent=6 block=36bdbe27
      "event. Strong southerly winds combined with robust solar " {i}
[247] indent=6 block=36bdbe27
      "irradiance during daylight hours pushed generation well above " {i}
[248] indent=6 block=36bdbe27
      "local load, creating significant negative-price hours in the DA " {i}
[249] indent=6 block=36bdbe27
      "market.\n[Followed by a DA vs. RT price table covering HE9–HE18 " {i}
[250] indent=6 block=36bdbe27
      "across HB_WEST, HB_NORTH, and HB_HOUSTON, then three drivers: " {i}
[251] indent=6 block=36bdbe27
      "wind, solar, transmission congestion]" {i}
[252] indent=0 block=-
[253] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "\nHB_WEST was negative or near-zero for 10 consecutive hours " {i}
[254] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "(HE9–HE18 CDT), while HB_NORTH and HB_HOUSTON were clearing " {i}
[255] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "$14–$38/MWh during the same window. That's a massive basis spread " {i}
[256] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "driven by local congestion.”" {i}
[257] indent=0 block=-
[258] indent=4 block=36bdbe27
      "▾ "
      "Bad"
[259] indent=6 block=36bdbe27
      "Question:" {b}
      " "
[260] indent=0 block=-
[261] indent=6 block=36bdbe27
      "\"For ERCOT operating day 2026-05-15, which Load Zone is forecasted" {i}
[262] indent=6 block=36bdbe27
      "to have the highest peak load, and which hours?\"" {i}
[263] indent=0 block=-
[264] indent=6 block=36bdbe27
      "Response:" {b}
[265] indent=0 block=-
[266] indent=6 block=36bdbe27
      "“The load profiles are charted above. NORTH_ERCOT's dominance is " {i}
[267] indent=6 block=36bdbe27
      "clear throughout the day, with the gap widening significantly from" {i}
[268] indent=6 block=36bdbe27
      "HE14 onward into the evening peak. Let me know if you want to " {i}
[269] indent=6 block=36bdbe27
      "cross-reference with RT actuals or DA prices for that zone.”" {i}
[270] indent=0 block=-
[271] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "Reviewer Comment:" {b}
[272] indent=0 block=-
[273] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "“No chart outputted. The answer never states which zone has the " {i}
[274] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "highest peak load or which hours. \"NORTH_ERCOT's dominance is " {i}
[275] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "clear throughout the day\" implies it's the answer, but the " {i}
[276] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "question asked for a specific zone and specific hours. neither is " {i}
[277] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "stated explicitly. A reader who needs this for a DA bid can't act " {i}
[278] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "on \"dominance is clear.””" {i}
[279] indent=0 block=-
