[301] indent=6 block=36bdbe27
      "Question:" {b}
[302] indent=0 block=-
[303] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "\"How did ERCOT real-time prices settle relative to DA forecasts by" {i}
[304] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "hub on 2026-05-15?”" {i}
[305] indent=0 block=-
[306] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "Response:" {b}
[307] indent=0 block=-
[308] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "Here's the DA vs. RT settlement picture for May 15." {i}
[309] indent=0 block=-
[310] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "Key themes:" {b i}
[311] indent=0 block=-
[312] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "West/Panhandle — RT ran well above DA overnight, then flipped" {b i}
[313] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "\nHB_WEST and HB_PAN were the most notable deviations. RT beat DA by" {i}
[314] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "$17–19/MWh in the overnight hours (HE1–HE8), likely reflecting " {i}
[315] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "lower-than-forecast wind output when DA priced in strong " {i}
[316] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "generation. Both hubs then flipped negative in the evening " {i}
[317] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "(HE19–HE20) before spiking again at HE22–HE24." {i}
[318] indent=0 block=-
[319] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "South — persistent RT discount through the afternoon" {b i}
      "\nHB_SOUTH was " {i}
[320] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "the weakest performer relative to DA. RT ran $10–15/MWh below DA " {i}
[321] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "from HE10 through HE16 — solar likely overperformed DA " {i}
[322] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "expectations, suppressing real-time prices. The daily average gap " {i}
[323] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "was -$5.48/MWh, the largest negative DART of any hub." {i}
[324] indent=0 block=-
[325] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "Houston — RT outperformed DA in the afternoon peak" {b i}
      "\nHB_HOUSTON was " {i}
[326] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "the only load-zone hub to finish the day with a positive DART " {i}
[327] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "(+$0.93/MWh). The afternoon ramp (HE15–HE18) saw RT exceed DA by " {i}
[328] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "up to $14.52/MWh, pointing to tighter supply conditions in the " {i}
[329] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "Houston pocket than the DA anticipated." {i}
[330] indent=0 block=-
[331] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "North — roughly flat on the day" {b i}
      "\nHB_NORTH tracked DA closely, with a" {i}
[332] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "modest -$0.87/MWh daily average. The afternoon hours showed mild " {i}
[333] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "RT premiums, but midday solar suppression offset those gains." {i}
[334] indent=0 block=-
[335] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────" {fg=#9b9a97}
[336] indent=0 block=-
